    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33143" root="فحل" body-key="f">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحَلَ الإِبِلَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحَلَ</span></b> , [inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحْلٌ</span>,] <i>He sent a
male</i> [meaning <i>a stallion-camel</i>] <i>among the</i> [<i>she-</i>]
<i>camels.</i> (S, O, K.) The inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحْلٌ</span> [used alone]

means The <i>putting a he-camel among the she-camels.</i> (KL.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحَلَ إِبِلَهُ فَحْلًا كَرِيمًا</span>
<i>He chose for his</i> [<i>she-</i>] <i>camels a generous male</i> [or
<i>stallion</i>]; as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">افتحل</span></b> . (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also the
next paragraph.

